<title>BELGIUM: East Europe oilseeds surplus seen tripling by 2005.</title>
<headline>East Europe oilseeds surplus seen tripling by 2005.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eastern Europe's oilseeds export surplus is expected to rise to nearly 900,000 tonnes in 2005 from 288,000 tonnes in 1994, European Commission projections showed.</p>
<p>The increase in 10 East European countries seeking EU membership is expected as a result of higher plantings even though farmers will have to respect EU set-aside rules after joining.</p>
<p>Output is seen growing to 5.2 million tonnes in 2005 from 3.6 million in 1994.</p>
<p>By contrast, the EU's oilseeds deficit is expected during the same period to grow to 16.2 million tonnes from 11.6 million, according to long-term projections by the Commission's agriculture department.</p>
<p>--Brussels Bureau +322 2876830</p>
</text>
